<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Datia State</h1><p class="st-meta">1626 CE – 1950 CE (approx.) · capital Datia</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Bundela Rajput state of Bundelkhand, famed for the seven-storey palace built by Bir Singh Deo of Orchha.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Datia was granted in 1626 to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bhagwan-rao-of-datia">Bhagwan Rao</a>, a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vir-singh-deo">Bir Singh Deo of Orchha</a>, making it a branch of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/orchha-state">Orchha State</a>. Bir Singh Deo had already built the great palace at Datia, completed around 1614.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharaja">Maharajas</a> served the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughals</a> as mansabdars and later contended with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Marathas</a>. In 1804 Datia made a treaty with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a> and became a salute state of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bundelkhand-agency">Bundelkhand Agency</a>. Its economy rested on agriculture, and the town grew around the palace and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pitambara-peeth">Pitambara Peeth</a> temple.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Datia joined <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/vindhya-pradesh">Vindhya Pradesh</a> in 1948 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madhya-pradesh">Madhya Pradesh</a> in 1956. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/datia-palace">Datia Palace</a>, a landmark of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bundelas">Bundela</a> architecture, survives in the town.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/datia-state.jpg" alt="Datia State" width="320" height="196"><figcaption>Image: Great Britain India Office · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Datia-Samthar_map.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1626 CE – 1950 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>princely state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Datia</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Bhagwan Rao, Govind Singh</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Bundeli</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Datia</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1788&amp;focus=datia-state" aria-label="Datia State on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6756 1234 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Datia State lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7076 1490L7083 1501M7076 1490L7364 1601M7076 1490L7364 1602M7076 1490L7160 1530"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7083 1501h0M7364 1601h0M7364 1602h0M7160 1530h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7076 1490h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7076 1490h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Datia. <a href="/atlas?year=1788&amp;focus=datia-state">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
